IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 2487 of 2020
CITATION: (2021) 3 SCC 241
YEAR: 2021

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, Indu Malhotra, Indira Banerjee

PARTIES:
IREO Grace vs Abhishek Khanna

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Consumer Protection Act, 1986, Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 18 RERA, Section 14 Consumer Protection

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
concurrent remedies, rera vs consumer forum, occupancy certificate delay

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Affirmed that remedies under the Consumer Protection Act and RERA are concurrent; flat buyers who received delayed occupancy certificates have right to elect appropriate forum.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 18 RERA, Section 14 Consumer Protection.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

